[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Traxler Counterattack"]
[Variation "Traxler: 5.Bxf7+ Ke7 6.Bb3"]
[ECO "C57"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,hanging-piece"]
[Themes "king-safety,piece-activity"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Ng5 4... Bc5 5. Bxf7+ { The calm reply: take the pawn with check, then keep the extra material. This is what a prepared opponent plays. } 5... Ke7 { The king steps up to e7. It is odd, but it keeps the rooks connected and blocks nothing important. }
6. Bb3 (6. Bc4 6... Qe8 7. O-O 7... d6 8. Nc3 8... Nd4) (6. Bd5 6... Rf8 7. O-O 7... d6 8. Nf3 8... Bg4 9. Bxc6 9... bxc6) 6... Rf8 { Gets the rook off the h8 corner, where the knight would take it, and puts it on the half-open f-file. [%cal Gh8f8] } (6... h6? { Kicks the knight, but it does not work. } 7. Nf7 7... Qe8 8. Nxh8 8... Qxh8)
7. d3 (7. d4 7... Nxd4 8. Nc3 8... d6) (7. c3 7... d6) (7. Nc3 7... d6) (7. O-O 7... d6) (7. Nf3 7... d6) 7... d6 { Opens the bishop on c8 and covers e5. }
8. Nf3 (8. Be3 8... Nd4 9. Nf3 9... Bg4 10. Nbd2 10... Nxb3 11. axb3 11... Bxe3) (8. Nc3 8... Nd4 9. Be3 9... Qe8) 8... a5 { Threatens ...a4 to harass the bishop on b3, and gives Black space on the queenside. [%cal Ga5a4] }
9. c3 9... Qe8 { Gets the queen off the pinned diagonal and eyes the kingside. } 10. O-O 10... Bg4 { Pins the knight on f3 to the queen on d1 and develops the last piece. [%cal Gg4f3] } *
